<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror, Comedy, Action,</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> N/A</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Courier Gabriel travels to deliver an unknown SCP to Site-19 with complications along the way.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Gabriel starts off loading the SCP into his delivery truck, noting not to ask questions on what's inside. Everything goes smoothly (agents with him), until they are attacked by an unknown GOI. The agents are lost or killed and Gabriel must finish this one-day delivery with guns pointed at him in every direction.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> No one has really written about the Logistics Department. I hope to start with these guys and do a series of each department, small and big. All of them will have a tad of workplace comedy, danger, and horror to whatever they're dealing with. It's Ironic how &quot;Another Day&quot; in the Foundation can usually mean life or death, no matter who you are.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> As me anything, I'll answer. I always love to hear a good crit about how to improve. Be blunt. Bash as hard as you can. You'll find I have a thick skull.</p>

