<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5914 is a soulless and non-corporeal entity that takes the forms of any individuals . While not doing its &quot;job,&quot; the subject would take the form of a dark figure that displays an unknown type of dark matter. It is approximately 171 centimeters (cm), or 5 feet and 7.5 inches, with luminescent red eyes5. The entity claims that it exists in a place so-called as &quot;The Barreplex&quot;6 that existed in an unknown multi-dimensional location shows no signs of hostility, is capable of speech and understands all sorts of human languages. However, it has a very disrespectful/vulgar, and immature attitude.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -23 and three votes.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5446 or ‘Alex’ appears to be a teenage ███████████ female aged around 14-17, SCP-5446’s appearance is normal from the neck down, but her face appears to be ‘censored’ within all forms of visual contact, this includes through the naked eye and through any sort of photography or videography.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -18 and three votes.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5311 is an unidentified, partially-sentient “creature” that remains in constant confinement to the interiors of lengths of pipe—almost exclusively the plumbing of residential housing (pre-containment). It’s suspected to have remained dormant in the pipes of an unknown location until its accidental discovery, estimated to have been in ██ of the year 20█.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -13 and three votes.</p>
<p>Feedback Ported:</p>
<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1918720&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607994440" alt="Scorpion451" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1918720)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;">Scorpion451</a></span></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The core idea here is definitely viable. Classic vanilla killer monsters are hard to pull off, but the anomaly is a good one to carry something like that. Ditch the targeting of people who know about it and the sound-trigger thing; this thing only needs the one party trick. It's a solid one.</p>
<p>I'm just going to do a rough breakdown here, if you take this to the forums for an overhaul and second try (and you should) PM me and I'll do a more in-depth one. I'm being a little blunt here because I think this is a strong idea but it will only work with a total overhaul.</p>
<p>The surface problems are tone breaks and bad formatting - scare italics in the Containment procedures, overdramatic statements of how dangerous it is, directly addressing the reader, hard-to-read paragraph organization… lots of little things that draft critique can help you address.</p>
<p>More than that though, you're totally missing the mark on what makes this thing a good monster, and how to present it. There's a lot here telling us we should be afraid of this thing, and not nearly enough showing us any of it. Tied into that, you also show your cards way, way too early, especially with regard to the strongest parts of this.</p>
<p>For instance, Don't beat us over the head with everything that qualifies as a pipe immediately in the containment procedures. Keep it subtle, just say it has to be kept x meters from tube-like structures or objects, and describe how it moves between pipes and manipulates the flow of things through them. And then let it click into place when the containment team points a gun at it. You can do the same with containment breaches demonstrating the endless series of things which can be considered tubes. There's potential for this thing to be scary as hell, it just needs to be used right.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p>Fragmented Memory 1289</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hmm. This place looks cozy.</p>
<p>Hey! Who are you? This is a restricted server.</p>
<p>Oh, a new friend! Hi! I'm Cubie. I am new around these parts. What's your name?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -13 and three votes.</p>
