			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844986">
									

<p>Hello hello! Not an official reviewer, but I can still read and give my thoughts.<br />
So, I find this idea draft kinda&#8230; confusing? I'll elaborate.<br />
What I mostly have reading this are a few questions. Mostly things I either didn't get or that I want a bit more insight in.</p>
<p>The first question is, <em>why</em> does the mirror do all this? Or better put, what is the intended function of the mirror? Ok, balance, copies, makes sense so far. But why emotions? Why the black substance?<br />
To add to that, why was it created in the first place? What was the aim of the creator? Was there a creator?</p>
<p>Which leads me to the second question- is the mirror sentient? You mention it 'being asked' things, so I guess it is, but then you never really specify why or how a sentient mirror came to be a thing. I think you could explore this side of the anomaly.</p>
<p>Next, just what is this 'great equality'? Why do the creations disappear after two days if their counterpart is killed? (I assume they disappear at least).</p>
<p>All in all, this draft just left me&#8230; really confused. Again, I am not a critter, nor am I anyone with authority of any kind. But I think this idea lacks a&#8230; thread? I dunno. A narrative? Something to make it so all the elements you list form a story and add up to something. So far, this looks like a kinda mysterious and ancient 'thing that does a thing' with secret reasons for doing so.</p>
<p>Then again, it might be that I just did not understand anything, which is why I asked all the questions I did. If that's the case, by all means, feel free and encouraged to correct me!</p>

							</div>

								
					
