														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844980">
									

<p>Again, my main issue here is that this seems like a flat retelling of other ideas about Hell. Its conceptual nature and the manner of the punishments don't seem to innovate anything beyond things that your audience has already read or seen about Hell — what makes your vision special?</p>
<p>Additionally your narrative seems less linear and more obsessed with the environment's atmosphere, which usually only works for an SCP if the environment is something novel. If there are explorations of Hell, what do they uncover? What do they add to the article?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A dead spy who had information the Foundation needed was a good motive for it to start using this SCP. Is there a problem in using the Insurgency?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It just seems odd to reference the GOI when they're not involved with the story.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>P.S.: Is MTF Psi-8 &quot;Silencers&quot; the right group for this SCP?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not likely. Silencers deal with ghosts on earth and sending them to their afterlives, and aren't very combat-heavy.</p>

							</div>

								
					
